Android: disable OpenCV Android sample subprojects

OpenCV 4.6.0 unconditionally adds samples/android/* subdirectories when
CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME is Android. Those CMakeLists call add_android_project(),
a helper that is only defined in a specific OpenCV-Android-SDK setup we
are not using. Result:
    CMake Error at samples/android/15-puzzle/CMakeLists.txt:3:
      Unknown CMake command "add_android_project"

Explicitly disable the two relevant toggles. BUILD_EXAMPLES=OFF alone
is insufficient — Android projects have their own gate.

Retire-if: upstream bumps OpenCV past a version where these
subdirectories are gated behind BUILD_EXAMPLES, or we drop OpenCV
from libslic3r's link set.

---
diff --git a/deps/OpenCV/OpenCV.cmake b/deps/OpenCV/OpenCV.cmake
index ad8c0a3585..efeb486f52 100644
--- a/deps/OpenCV/OpenCV.cmake
+++ b/deps/OpenCV/OpenCV.cmake
@@ -18,6 +18,8 @@ orcaslicer_add_cmake_project(OpenCV
        -DBUILD_TESTS=OFF
        -DBUILD_opencv_python_tests=OFF
        -DBUILD_EXAMPLES=OFF
+       -DBUILD_ANDROID_PROJECTS=OFF
+       -DBUILD_ANDROID_EXAMPLES=OFF
        -DBUILD_JASPER=OFF
        -DBUILD_JAVA=OFF
        -DBUILD_JPEG=ON
